<title>USA: Citicorp unit files $4 billion shelf.</title>
<headline>Citicorp unit files $4 billion shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mortgage Capital Funding Inc, a unit of Citicorp, filed Thursday a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $4 billion in mortgage pass-through securities.</p>
<p>When combined with a previous registration, Mortgage Capital will have a total offering of $4,781,873,799 in securities available for sale.  </p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to purchase mortgage loans and to pay certain expenses in connection with the issuance of the certificates, the company said in the filing.</p>
</text>
